{# Transcribed from the static design mockup (checkout page)'s <main> grid. Extends
   layouts/checkout.twig, whose <main class="lg:grid lg:grid-cols-2"> wrapper matches
   this page's own <main> class from the mockup exactly (this layout serves only the
   checkout page). Header/footer are the layout's partials/header-checkout.twig and
   partials/footer-compliance.twig includes.

   DEVIATION (locked business decision): the CONSENT checkboxes below ship WITHOUT
   the `checked` attribute the mockup pre-checks them with — consent is an explicit
   affirmative action, so nothing here is ever pre-ticked.

   DEVIATION: the mockup's shipping-method selector (two DHL options at $7.50 and
   $12.50) is gone, along with the shipping and tax rows of its totals block. This
   theme prices all-inclusive: there is no shipping cost and no tax anywhere in the
   model, so a priced courier choice was a control that could never be charged for.

   DEVIATION: the mockup's state <select> carried no `value` attributes, so its
   options would have posted "New York" where the server expects "NY". The codes are
   the values here, and the five inhabited US territories the server accepts are in
   the list too.

   DEVIATION: four of the mockup's controls are gone because nothing behind them
   could store what was typed in — a box that silently discards its own value is
   worse than no box. They are the "Company (optional)" and "Apartment, suite, etc.
   (optional)" fields (the order carries one address line), the "Use shipping address
   as billing address" checkbox (billing IS shipping, so it is now a stated line
   rather than a choice), and the "Notify me with news and offers" checkbox in
   Contact (the marketing consent below owns that answer, and two controls for one
   permission is how they come to disagree).

   Image srcs → /assets/img/...; "Apple Pay.svg" is renamed apple-pay-badge.svg in the
   theme's asset set. payment-icons.svg, PayPal.svg, paypal-logo.svg, afterpay-logo.svg,
   usa.svg keep their mockup names. Product images come from the catalog; a product
   with none keeps the mockup's placeholder icon tile.

   Inline scripts extracted to theme/js/checkout.js: the payment-panel show/hide sync
   is verbatim; the mockup's "Pay Now" navigation handler is gone now that the form
   posts for real. #}
{% extends 'layouts/checkout.twig' %}
{% set page_title = 'Checkout' %}
{% set page_description = 'Complete your AsterMD order: choose a treatment plan, delivery, and payment.' %}
{% block content %}

  {# ONE form for the whole page, spanning both columns of the layout's
     `<main>` grid. A form cannot be nested in another form, so the summary
     column's sub-actions (plan switch, promo apply/remove, bump) used to be
     sibling forms carrying the buyer's fields again as hidden inputs — which
     meant a bump toggle posted whatever the server last rendered and wrote it
     back over what the buyer had since typed. Here each sub-action is a submit
     button that redirects this one form with `formaction`, so it posts exactly
     what is in the boxes right now, with no script involved ([27.10], [8.7]).

     `contents` keeps the two column divs as the grid items of `<main>`, the
     way partials/cart-remove-form.twig already spans a grid row. #}
  <form method="post" action="{{ url('/checkout') }}" id="checkout-form" data-checkout-form novalidate class="contents">
    <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{{ csrf_token }}" />

    {# Pressing Enter in a text field submits a form's *first* submit
       button, wherever the cursor is. With one form spanning the page that
       would otherwise be Pay Now, so typing a discount code and pressing
       Enter would charge the card at full price. This button is first in tree
       order and applies the code instead: Enter in the discount box does what
       the buyer meant, Enter anywhere else re-renders and keeps everything
       typed, and no keystroke can place an order. Paying is only ever a click
       on Pay Now. #}
    <button type="submit" formaction="{{ url('/checkout/promo') }}" class="sr-only" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">Apply discount code</button>

  <!-- ==================== CHECKOUT FORM ==================== -->
  <div class="px-6 py-10 sm:px-10 lg:px-16 lg:py-14">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[500px] lg:mx-0 lg:ml-auto">

      <!-- ==================== EXPRESS CHECKOUT ==================== -->
      <p class="text-center text-sm text-muted">Express checkout</p>
      <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3">
        <button type="button" class="flex items-center justify-center transition-opacity hover:opacity-90">
          <img src="/assets/img/PayPal.svg" alt="Pay with PayPal" class="h-12 w-auto max-w-full" />
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="flex items-center justify-center transition-opacity hover:opacity-90">
          <img src="/assets/img/apple-pay-badge.svg" alt="Pay with Apple Pay" class="h-12 w-auto max-w-full" />
        </button>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-6 flex items-center gap-4">
        <span class="h-px flex-1 bg-border"></span>
        <span class="text-sm text-muted">OR</span>
        <span class="h-px flex-1 bg-border"></span>
      </div>

      {% if checkout.notice %}
      <p role="alert" class="mt-6 rounded-sm border border-danger bg-background px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-danger">{{ checkout.notice }}</p>
      {% endif %}

      <!-- ==================== CONTACT ==================== -->
      <h2 class="mt-5 font-heading text-base font-bold sm:text-lg text-heading">Contact</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 flex flex-col gap-4">
        <div class="relative">
          <input type="email" id="checkout-email" name="email" value="{{ checkout.prefill.email|default('') }}" autocomplete="email" placeholder=" " class="field-input w-full rounded-sm border border-border bg-background px-4 text-sm text-heading"
            {% if checkout.errors.email|default(null) %}aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="checkout-error-email"{% endif %} />
          <label for="checkout-email" class="field-label">Email</label>
          {% include 'partials/checkout/field-error.twig' with { field: 'email' } %}
        </div>

        <div class="relative">
          <input type="tel" id="checkout-phone" name="phone" value="{{ checkout.prefill.phone|default('') }}" autocomplete="tel" placeholder=" " class="field-input w-full rounded-sm border border-border bg-background px-4 pr-16 text-sm text-heading"
            {% if checkout.errors.phone|default(null) %}aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="checkout-error-phone"{% endif %} />
          <span class="pointer-events-none absolute right-4 top-1/2 flex -translate-y-1/2 items-center gap-1 text-base text-muted" aria-hidden="true">
            <img src="/assets/img/usa.svg" alt="" class="h-[19px] w-[34px] rounded-[2px]" />
            <i data-lucide="chevron-down" class="size-4"></i>
          </span>
          <label for="checkout-phone" class="field-label">Phone</label>
          {% include 'partials/checkout/field-error.twig' with { field: 'phone' } %}
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ==================== DELIVERY ==================== -->
      <h2 class="mt-8 font-heading text-base font-bold sm:text-lg text-heading">Delivery</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 flex flex-col gap-4">
        <div class="relative">
          <label for="checkout-country" class="sr-only">Country</label>
          {# No `name`: the country is fixed ([13.36] is a declared gap), and the
             server's territory set says the same thing. It stays on the page
             because a delivery block with no country reads as an omission. #}
          <select id="checkout-country" class="focus-ring-primary h-12 w-full appearance-none rounded-sm border border-border bg-background px-4 py-0 pr-10 text-sm text-heading">
            <option>United States</option>
          </select>
          <i data-lucide="chevron-down" class="pointer-events-none absolute right-4 top-1/2 size-4 -translate-y-1/2 text-heading"></i>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="relative">
            <input type="text" id="checkout-first-name" name="first_name" value="{{ checkout.prefill.first_name|default('') }}" autocomplete="given-name" placeholder=" " class="field-input w-full rounded-sm border border-border bg-background px-4 text-sm text-heading"
              {% if checkout.errors.first_name|default(null) %}aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="checkout-error-first_name"{% endif %} />
            <label for="checkout-first-name" class="field-label">First name</label>
            {% include 'partials/checkout/field-error.twig' with { field: 'first_name' } %}
          </div>
          <div class="relative">
            <input type="text" id="checkout-last-name" name="last_name" value="{{ checkout.prefill.last_name|default('') }}" autocomplete="family-name" placeholder=" " class="field-input w-full rounded-sm border border-border bg-background px-4 text-sm text-heading"
              {% if checkout.errors.last_name|default(null) %}aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="checkout-error-last_name"{% endif %} />
            <label for="checkout-last-name" class="field-label">Last name</label>
            {% include 'partials/checkout/field-error.twig' with { field: 'last_name' } %}
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="relative">
          <input type="text" id="checkout-address" name="address_line" value="{{ checkout.prefill.address_line|default('') }}" autocomplete="street-address" placeholder=" " class="field-input w-full rounded-sm border border-border bg-background px-4 pr-10 text-sm text-heading"
            {% if checkout.errors.address_line|default(null) %}aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="checkout-error-address_line"{% endif %} />
          <i data-lucide="search" class="pointer-events-none absolute right-4 top-1/2 size-4 -translate-y-1/2 text-icon-muted"></i>
          <label for="checkout-address" class="field-label">Address</label>
          {% include 'partials/checkout/field-error.twig' with { field: 'address_line' } %}
        </div>

        <div class="relative">
          <input type="text" id="checkout-city" name="city" value="{{ checkout.prefill.city|default('') }}" autocomplete="address-level2" placeholder=" " class="field-input w-full rounded-sm border border-border bg-background px-4 text-sm text-heading"
            {% if checkout.errors.city|default(null) %}aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="checkout-error-city"{% endif %} />
          <label for="checkout-city" class="field-label">City</label>
          {% include 'partials/checkout/field-error.twig' with { field: 'city' } %}
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="relative">
            <label for="checkout-state" class="sr-only">State</label>
            {% set territories = {
              'AL': 'Alabama', 'AK': 'Alaska', 'AZ': 'Arizona', 'AR': 'Arkansas', 'CA': 'California',
              'CO': 'Colorado', 'CT': 'Connecticut', 'DE': 'Delaware', 'DC': 'District of Columbia',
              'FL': 'Florida', 'GA': 'Georgia', 'HI': 'Hawaii', 'ID': 'Idaho', 'IL': 'Illinois',
              'IN': 'Indiana', 'IA': 'Iowa', 'KS': 'Kansas', 'KY': 'Kentucky', 'LA': 'Louisiana',
              'ME': 'Maine', 'MD': 'Maryland', 'MA': 'Massachusetts', 'MI': 'Michigan', 'MN': 'Minnesota',
              'MS': 'Mississippi', 'MO': 'Missouri', 'MT': 'Montana', 'NE': 'Nebraska', 'NV': 'Nevada',
              'NH': 'New Hampshire', 'NJ': 'New Jersey', 'NM': 'New Mexico', 'NY': 'New York',
              'NC': 'North Carolina', 'ND': 'North Dakota', 'OH': 'Ohio', 'OK': 'Oklahoma', 'OR': 'Oregon',
              'PA': 'Pennsylvania', 'RI': 'Rhode Island', 'SC': 'South Carolina', 'SD': 'South Dakota',
              'TN': 'Tennessee', 'TX': 'Texas', 'UT': 'Utah', 'VT': 'Vermont', 'VA': 'Virginia',
              'WA': 'Washington', 'WV': 'West Virginia', 'WI': 'Wisconsin', 'WY': 'Wyoming',
              'AS': 'American Samoa', 'GU': 'Guam', 'MP': 'Northern Mariana Islands',
              'PR': 'Puerto Rico', 'VI': 'U.S. Virgin Islands'
            } %}
            <select id="checkout-state" name="territory" autocomplete="address-level1" class="focus-ring-primary h-12 w-full appearance-none rounded-sm border border-border bg-background px-4 py-0 pr-10 text-sm text-heading"
              {% if checkout.errors.territory|default(null) %}aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="checkout-error-territory"{% endif %}>
              <option value="">Choose your state</option>
              {% for code, name in territories %}
              <option value="{{ code }}"{% if checkout.prefill.territory|default('') == code %} selected{% endif %}>{{ name }}</option>
              {% endfor %}
            </select>
            <i data-lucide="chevron-down" class="pointer-events-none absolute right-4 top-1/2 size-4 -translate-y-1/2 text-heading"></i>
            {% include 'partials/checkout/field-error.twig' with { field: 'territory' } %}
          </div>
          <div class="relative">
            <input type="text" id="checkout-postal" name="postal_code" value="{{ checkout.prefill.postal_code|default('') }}" autocomplete="postal-code" placeholder=" " class="field-input w-full rounded-sm border border-border bg-background px-4 text-sm text-heading"
              {% if checkout.errors.postal_code|default(null) %}aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="checkout-error-postal_code"{% endif %} />
            <label for="checkout-postal" class="field-label">Postal code</label>
            {% include 'partials/checkout/field-error.twig' with { field: 'postal_code' } %}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ==================== PAYMENT ==================== -->
      <h2 class="mt-8 font-heading text-base font-bold sm:text-lg text-heading">Payment</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted">All transactions are secure and encrypted.</p>

      {# [15.4c]: the payment section is provider-dependent and cannot be a fixed
         block of markup, so it is a slot the adapter fills. The configured
         provider collects cards in the theme's own fields; a tokenizing one
         hosts its own surface, and gets the second branch without this template
         being rewritten. #}
      {% if checkout.capabilities.rendersOwnCardFields %}
      <div class="mt-3.5 overflow-hidden rounded-md border border-border bg-background" data-select-group id="payment-method-group">
        <div class="border-b border-border">
          <button type="button" data-select-option data-payment="card" aria-pressed="true" class="group flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-3 rounded-t-md bg-background p-3 text-left transition-colors aria-pressed:bg-primary-light">
            <span class="flex items-center gap-3">
              <span class="flex w-[18px] h-[18px] shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border-2 border-border-darker group-aria-pressed:border-primary">
                <span class="size-2 rounded-full group-aria-pressed:bg-primary"></span>
              </span>
              <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-heading">Credit card</span>
            </span>
            <span class="flex shrink-0 items-center">
              <img src="/assets/img/payment-icons.svg" alt="Mastercard, Visa, Amex, Discover" class="h-6 w-auto" />
            </span>
          </button>
          <div data-payment-panel="card" class="flex flex-col gap-4 border-t border-border bg-background-2 px-5 py-5">
            {# No value attribute on any of the three, ever. The buyer's contact
               details are preserved so the form re-fills after a decline
               ([13.30]); the card is not a contact detail ([15.8]). #}
            <div class="relative">
              <input type="text" id="checkout-card-number" name="card_number" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="cc-number" placeholder=" " class="field-input w-full rounded-sm border border-border bg-background px-4 pr-10 text-sm text-heading" />
              <i data-lucide="lock" class="pointer-events-none absolute right-4 top-1/2 size-4 -translate-y-1/2 text-icon-muted"></i>
              <label for="checkout-card-number" class="field-label">Card number</label>
            </div>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
              <div class="relative">
                <input type="text" id="checkout-card-expiry" name="card_expiry" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="cc-exp" placeholder=" " class="field-input w-full rounded-sm border border-border bg-background px-4 text-sm text-heading" />
                <label for="checkout-card-expiry" class="field-label">Expiration date (MM / YY)</label>
              </div>
              <div class="relative">
                <input type="text" id="checkout-card-cvc" name="card_cvc" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="cc-csc" placeholder=" " class="field-input w-full rounded-sm border border-border bg-background px-4 pr-10 text-sm text-heading" />
                <i data-lucide="circle-help" class="pointer-events-none absolute right-4 top-1/2 size-4 -translate-y-1/2 text-icon-muted"></i>
                <label for="checkout-card-cvc" class="field-label">Security code</label>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="relative">
              <input type="text" id="checkout-card-name" autocomplete="cc-name" placeholder=" " class="field-input w-full rounded-sm border border-border bg-background px-4 text-sm text-heading" />
              <label for="checkout-card-name" class="field-label">Name on card</label>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted">Billing address is the delivery address above.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="border-b border-border">
          <button type="button" data-select-option data-payment="paypal" aria-pressed="false" class="group flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-3 bg-background p-3 text-left transition-colors aria-pressed:bg-primary-light">
            <span class="flex items-center gap-3">
              <span class="flex w-[18px] h-[18px] shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border-2 border-border-darker group-aria-pressed:border-primary">
                <span class="size-2 rounded-full group-aria-pressed:bg-primary"></span>
              </span>
              <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-heading">PayPal</span>
            </span>
            <img src="/assets/img/paypal-logo.svg" alt="PayPal" class="h-3.5 w-auto shrink-0" />
          </button>
        </div>

        <div>
          <button type="button" data-select-option data-payment="afterpay" aria-pressed="false" class="group flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-3 rounded-b-md bg-background p-3 text-left transition-colors aria-pressed:bg-primary-light">
            <span class="flex items-center gap-3">
              <span class="flex w-[18px] h-[18px] shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border-2 border-border-darker group-aria-pressed:border-primary">
                <span class="size-2 rounded-full group-aria-pressed:bg-primary"></span>
              </span>
              <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-heading">Afterpay</span>
            </span>
            <img src="/assets/img/afterpay-logo.svg" alt="Afterpay" class="h-3.5 w-auto shrink-0" />
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
      {% else %}
      <div class="mt-3.5 overflow-hidden rounded-md border border-border bg-background p-5" data-payment-surface>
        {# The provider hosts its own card fields. Nothing of the card is ours to
           render, to name, or to see. #}
        <div id="payment-provider-surface" data-provider="{{ checkout.capabilities.providerCategory }}"></div>
        <noscript>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted">Your payment provider's secure card form needs JavaScript to load.</p>
        </noscript>
      </div>
      {% endif %}

      <!-- ==================== CONSENT + SUBMIT ==================== -->
      {# [26.2]: consent is an explicit affirmative action, so no control here
         ever carries a `checked` attribute — not on a first render, and not on
         a re-render after a decline. The copy is operator-authored config
         rather than visitor input, which is what makes |raw safe. #}
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col gap-4">
        {% for consent in checkout.consents %}
        <label class="flex cursor-pointer items-start gap-3 rounded-md border {% if checkout.errors[consent.key]|default(null) %}border-danger{% else %}border-border{% endif %} px-5 py-4">
          {# The red border below is the only thing that said "this one" to a
             sighted buyer; these two attributes say it to everybody else, and
             they are the same pair every other control on this page carries.
             The id is the one partials/checkout/field-error.twig emits, so the
             message the buyer is sent to is the message actually rendered. #}
          <input type="checkbox" class="peer sr-only" name="consents[{{ consent.key }}]" value="on" data-consent="{{ consent.key }}"
            {% if checkout.errors[consent.key]|default(null) %}aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="checkout-error-{{ consent.key }}"{% endif %} />
          <span class="mt-0.5 flex size-4 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded border border-border-darker bg-background transition-colors peer-checked:border-primary peer-checked:bg-primary">
            <i data-lucide="check" class="size-3 text-background" stroke-width="3"></i>
          </span>
          <span class="text-sm text-body">{{ consent.html|raw }}</span>
        </label>
        {% include 'partials/checkout/field-error.twig' with { field: consent.key } %}
        {% endfor %}
      </div>

      {# `data-checkout-submit` marks this button, and only this button, as the
         one that places the order. theme/js/checkout.js hooks it by that attribute to
         put it in a busy state while the order posts, so an impatient second click has
         nothing to click. The hook stays off every `formaction` button on purpose: a
         promo apply or a plan switch must stay live so the buyer can keep editing.

         `data-busy-label` is the text the script swaps in, so the button keeps a real
         accessible name in the busy state and the state reads without relying on
         colour. `aria-busy:` styles the same state visually, from the same attribute.

         This is comfort, not correctness. The button works with the script absent, and
         no script can stop a reload, a browser retry or a second tab from posting this
         form twice — only the server can ([8.7]). #}
      <button type="submit" id="checkout-pay" data-checkout-submit data-busy-label="Placing order…" class="mt-6 flex h-[41px] w-full items-center justify-center rounded-sm bg-primary px-5 text-base font-medium text-primary-foreground transition-colors hover:bg-primary-hover focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary-hover aria-busy:cursor-progress aria-busy:opacity-75 sm:h-[41px]">
        Pay Now
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ==================== ORDER SUMMARY ==================== -->
  <div class="border-border bg-background-2 px-6 py-10 sm:px-10 lg:border-l lg:px-12 lg:py-14">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[410px] lg:mx-0 lg:sticky lg:top-10">

      <!-- ==================== TREATMENT PLAN SELECTOR ==================== -->
      {% if checkout.plans %}
      <h2 class="font-heading text-base font-bold sm:text-lg text-heading">Select Treatment Plan</h2>
      <p class="mt-0.5 text-xs text-muted">{{ checkout.plans.name }}</p>

      {# The plan slug is the same for every option, so it is one hidden input
         outside the loop; the variant rides on each button as its own
         name/value, so only the option actually clicked is submitted. #}
      <input type="hidden" name="slug" value="{{ checkout.plans.slug }}" />
      <div class="mt-3.5 flex flex-col gap-2 rounded-md border border-border bg-background overflow-hidden" data-select-group>
        {% for option in checkout.plans.options %}
        <button type="submit" formaction="{{ url('/checkout/plan') }}" name="variant_id" value="{{ option.id }}" data-select-option aria-pressed="{{ option.id == checkout.plans.chosen ? 'true' : 'false' }}" class="group flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-3 rounded-md border border-transparent p-3 text-left transition-colors hover:border-primary/40 aria-pressed:border-primary aria-pressed:bg-primary-light">
          <span class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="flex mt-1 w-[18px] h-[18px] shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border-2 border-border-darker group-aria-pressed:border-primary">
              <span class="size-2 rounded-full group-aria-pressed:bg-primary"></span>
            </span>
            <span>
              <span class="block text-sm font-semibold text-heading">{{ option.name }}</span>
              <span class="block text-sm text-muted mt-1">Billed once</span>
            </span>
          </span>
          <span class="shrink-0 text-sm font-semibold text-heading">{{ option.price_cents|money }}</span>
        </button>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% endif %}

      <!-- ==================== LINE ITEMS ==================== -->
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-4">
        {% for line in checkout.lines %}
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <div class="relative shrink-0">
            {% if line.image %}
            <img src="{{ line.image }}" alt="{{ line.name }}" class="size-14 rounded-sm object-cover" />
            {% else %}
            <span class="flex size-14 items-center justify-center rounded-sm bg-surface">
              <i data-lucide="pill" class="size-6 text-icon-muted"></i>
            </span>
            {% endif %}
            <span class="absolute -right-1.5 -top-1.5 flex size-5 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-heading text-xs font-medium text-background">{{ line.quantity }}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex-1">
            <p class="text-sm text-heading">{{ line.name }}</p>
            {% if line.variant_name %}
            <p class="mt-0.5 flex items-center gap-1 text-sm text-muted">
              <i data-lucide="refresh-cw" class="size-3.5"></i>
              {{ line.variant_name }}
            </p>
            {% endif %}
          </div>
          {# A free attachment shows at 0¢ rather than being hidden: a supply the
             buyer is receiving belongs on the summary whether or not it is
             charged for ([7.14a]). #}
          <p class="shrink-0 text-base font-medium text-heading">{{ line.line_total_cents|money }}</p>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>

      <!-- ==================== DISCOUNT CODE ==================== -->
      {# [13.18], [14.4]: hidden outright when the active adapter declares no
         promotion support, rather than shown and failing at runtime. #}
      {% if checkout.capabilities.supportsPromotions %}
      {% if checkout.promotion %}
      <div class="mt-6 flex items-center justify-between gap-3 rounded-sm border border-border bg-background px-4 py-3">
        <span class="text-sm text-heading">Discount <span class="font-semibold">{{ checkout.promotion.code }}</span> applied</span>
        <button type="submit" formaction="{{ url('/checkout/promo/remove') }}" class="shrink-0 text-sm font-medium text-primary underline hover:text-primary-hover">Remove</button>
      </div>
      {% else %}
      <div class="mt-6 flex gap-3">
        <label for="checkout-discount" class="sr-only">Discount code or gift card</label>
        <input type="text" id="checkout-discount" name="discount_code" placeholder="Discount code or gift card" class="focus-ring-primary h-12 min-w-0 flex-1 rounded-sm border border-border bg-background px-4 py-0 text-sm text-heading placeholder:text-sm placeholder:text-body" />
        <button type="submit" formaction="{{ url('/checkout/promo') }}" class="flex h-12 items-center justify-center shrink-0 rounded-sm border border-border bg-background px-6 text-base font-medium text-heading transition-colors hover:border-primary hover:text-primary">Apply</button>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% endif %}

      <!-- ==================== TOTALS ==================== -->
      {# No shipping and no tax rows: [13.35] is a declared gap, so the total is
         exactly subtotal minus discount, in integer cents. #}
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col gap-2 border-t border-border pt-6 text-[14px] text-heading">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <span>Subtotal • {{ checkout.itemCount }} item{{ checkout.itemCount == 1 ? '' : 's' }}</span>
          <span>{{ checkout.totals.subtotalCents|money }}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <span>Consultation Fee</span>
          <span>Included</span>
        </div>
        {% if checkout.totals.discountCents > 0 %}
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <span>Discount{% if checkout.promotion %} • {{ checkout.promotion.code }}{% endif %}</span>
          <span>−{{ checkout.totals.discountCents|money }}</span>
        </div>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
      <div class="mt-4 flex items-center justify-between border-t border-border pt-4">
        <span class="text-base font-medium sm:text-lg text-heading">Total</span>
        <span class="text-base font-medium sm:text-lg text-heading"><span class="mr-1 text-sm font-normal text-muted align-middle">{{ checkout.currency }}</span>{{ checkout.totals.totalCents|money }}</span>
      </div>

      <!-- ==================== PAYMENT AUTHORIZATION NOTICE ==================== -->
      <div class="mt-6 flex items-start gap-3 rounded-sm border border-primary bg-primary-light px-4 py-4">
        <i data-lucide="info" class="mt-0.5 size-5 shrink-0 text-primary"></i>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-heading">Payment authorization will be held; you will only be charged if approved and prescribed by a doctor.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- ==================== ORDER BUMPS ==================== -->
      {# §27: an accepted bump is an ordinary cart line on the main charge, not a
         second order. Each "Add" is a submit button on the page's one form, so
         accepting one posts the buyer's details exactly as they are typed right
         now: the summary changes without the buyer leaving the page or losing
         anything typed ([27.10]). #}
      {% if checkout.bumps %}
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-4">
        {% for bump in checkout.bumps %}
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          {% if bump.image %}
          <img src="{{ bump.image }}" alt="{{ bump.name }}" class="size-14 shrink-0 rounded-sm object-cover" />
          {% else %}
          <span class="flex size-14 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-sm bg-surface">
            <i data-lucide="pill" class="size-6 text-icon-muted"></i>
          </span>
          {% endif %}
          <div class="flex-1">
            <p class="text-sm text-heading">{{ bump.headline }}</p>
            {% if bump.body %}<p class="text-sm text-muted">{{ bump.body }}</p>{% endif %}
            <p class="text-sm text-muted">
              {{ bump.price_cents|money }}
              {% if bump.discounted %}<span class="ml-1 text-muted line-through">{{ bump.catalog_price_cents|money }}</span>{% endif %}
            </p>
          </div>
          {# The slug rides on the button so only the bump actually clicked is
             submitted; a hidden input per row would post every one of them. #}
          <button type="submit" formaction="{{ url('/checkout/bump') }}" name="bump_slug" value="{{ bump.slug }}" class="shrink-0 rounded-sm border border-border bg-background px-5 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-heading transition-colors hover:border-primary hover:text-primary">Add</button>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
  </form>

{% endblock %}
{% block scripts %}
{{ parent() }}
<script src="{{ asset('checkout.js') }}" defer></script>
{% endblock %}
